   "body": "Notation used above, collected in one place.",
   "attrs": {"title": "Conventions", "order": 9}},
  {"source":
   {"file": "blueprint/spaces/covers/_section.md", "anonymous": false},
   "kind": "section",
   "id": "covers",
   "depth": 0,
   "boundary": [],
   "body": "",
   "attrs": {"title": "Covers", "order": 1}},
  {"source": {"file": "blueprint/spaces/covers/opening.md", "anonymous": false},
   "kind": "hidden",
   "id": "covers-opening",
   "depth": 0,
   "boundary": [],
   "body":
   "Two notions recur below, and both are about families of subsets indexed by\nan arbitrary set $I$.",
   "attrs": {"order": 0}},
  {"source":
   {"file": "blueprint/spaces/compact/def-compact.md", "anonymous": false},
   "kind": "definition",
   "id": "def-compact",
   "depth": 0,
   "boundary": [],
   "body":
   "$X$ is *compact* when every open cover of $X$ ([def-cover]) has a finite\nsubcover.",
   "attrs": {"title": "Compact space", "order": 1}},
  {"source":
   {"file": "blueprint/spaces/covers/def-cover.md", "anonymous": false},
   "kind": "definition",
   "id": "def-cover",
   "depth": 0,
   "boundary": [],
   "body":
   "An *open cover* of $X$ is a family $\\fam{U} = (U_i)_{i \\in I}$ of open sets\nwith\n\n$$\n\\bigcup_{i \\in I} U_i = X .\n$$\n\nA *subcover* is a subfamily $(U_j)_{j \\in J}$, $J \\subseteq I$, that is\nstill a cover; it is *finite* when $J$ is.",
   "attrs": {"title": "Open cover", "order": 1}},
  {"source": {"file": "blueprint/spaces/covers/def-fip.md", "anonymous": false},
   "kind": "definition",
   "id": "def-fip",
   "depth": 0,
   "boundary": [],
   "body":
   "A family $(F_i)_{i \\in I}$ of subsets of $X$ has the *finite intersection\nproperty* when every finite subfamily meets:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF_{i_1} \\cap \\dots \\cap F_{i_n} &\\neq \\emptyset\n  &&\\text{for all } n \\ge 1 \\text{ and } i_1, \\dots, i_n \\in I .\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nIt is the dual of [def-cover] under complements.",
   "attrs": {"title": "Finite intersection property", "order": 2}},
  {"source": {"file": "blueprint/appendix/figure.md", "anonymous": false},
   "kind": "remark",
   "id": "figure-cover",
   "depth": 0,
   "boundary": [],
   "body":
   "The picture shows three open sets covering a compact interval; two of them\nalready suffice.\n\n![Three open intervals covering a closed interval](cover.png)",
   "attrs": {"title": "A finite subcover", "order": 2}},
  {"source": {"file": "blueprint/intro.md", "anonymous": false},
   "kind": "section",
   "id": "intro",
   "depth": 0,
   "boundary": [],
   "body":
   "We prove that a space is compact exactly when every family of closed sets\nwith the finite intersection property has a point in common\n([thm-fip]), and use it to show that a product of two compact spaces is\ncompact ([thm-product]).  The argument is the one in Čech's and Erdős'\nlecture notes, written so that every step can be checked on its own.\n\nThroughout, $X$ and $Y$ are topological spaces and $\\Opens{X}$ is the set of\nopen subsets of $X$.",
   "attrs": {"title": "Introduction", "order": 1}},
  {"source":
   {"file": "blueprint/spaces/compact/lem-complements.md", "anonymous": false},
   "kind": "lemma",
   "id": "lem-complements",
   "depth": 0,
   "boundary": [],
   "body":
   "For a family $(F_i)_{i \\in I}$ of closed sets put $U_i = X \\setminus F_i$.\nThen\n$$\n\\bigcap_{i \\in I} F_i = \\emptyset\n\\iff\n\\bigcup_{i \\in I} U_i = X ,\n$$\nso $(U_i)$ is an open cover exactly when the $F_i$ have no common point.",
   "attrs": {"title": "Complements", "order": 1}},
  {"source":
   {"file": "blueprint/spaces/compact/lem-finite-subfamily.md",
    "anonymous": false},
   "kind": "lemma",
   "id": "lem-finite-subfamily",
   "depth": 0,
   "boundary": [],
   "body":
   "For $J \\subseteq I$ finite, $(U_j)_{j \\in J}$ covers $X$ if and only if\n$\\bigcap_{j \\in J} F_j = \\emptyset$.  Hence $(U_i)$ has no finite subcover\nif and only if $(F_i)$ has the finite intersection property.",
   "attrs": {"title": "Finite subfamilies", "order": 2}},
  {"source":
   {"file": "blueprint/spaces/compact/lem-tube.md", "anonymous": false},
   "kind": "lemma",
   "id": "lem-tube",
   "depth": 0,
   "boundary": [],
   "body":
   "Let $Y$ be compact, $x \\in X$, and $W \\subseteq X \\times Y$ open with\n$\\{x\\} \\times Y \\subseteq W$.  Then there is an open $U \\ni x$ with\n$U \\times Y \\subseteq W$.",
   "attrs": {"title": "Tube lemma", "order": 4}},
  {"source": {"file": "blueprint/appendix/notation.md", "anonymous": false},
   "kind": "remark",
   "id": "notation",
   "depth": 0,
   "boundary": [],
   "body":
   "| Symbol | Meaning | First used |\n| :--- | :--- | ---: |\n| $\\cl{A}$ | the closure of $A$ | [def-fip] |\n| $\\Opens{X}$ | the open subsets of $X$ | [intro] |\n| $\\fam{U}$, $\\fam{W}$ | families of open sets | [def-cover] |\n| $\\Top$ | the category of spaces, $f\\colon X \\to Y$ continuous | — |\n\nGreek letters index families (α ∈ A), and ℝ, ≤, → are used as usual.\nIdentifiers in the Lean sources look like `TopologicalSpace.IsCompact` or\n`isCompact_iff_finite_subfamily_closed`; a typical lookup is\n\n```lean\nexample (X : Type*) [TopologicalSpace X] :\n    CompactSpace X ↔ IsCompact (Set.univ : Set X) := ⟨fun h => h.1, fun h => ⟨h⟩⟩\n```\n\n> Every result here is classical; see any text on point-set topology.",
   "attrs": {"title": "Symbols", "order": 1}},
  {"source": {"file": "blueprint/products/_section.md", "anonymous": false},
   "kind": "section",
   "id": "products",
   "depth": 0,
   "boundary": [],
   "body":
   "Finite products of compact spaces are compact.  The tube lemma\n([lem-tube]) is stated in Section [compact]; it is the whole content of the\nargument.",
   "attrs": {"title": "Products", "order": 3}},
  {"source":
   {"file": "blueprint/spaces/compact/lem-tube.proof.md", "anonymous": false},
   "kind": "proof",
   "id": "proof/lem-tube",
   "depth": 1,
   "boundary": [{"role": "of", "id": "lem-tube"}],
   "body":
   "Cover $\\{x\\} \\times Y$ by basic open sets $U_y \\times V_y \\subseteq W$.  The\n$V_y$ cover $Y$, so finitely many do, say $V_{y_1}, \\dots, V_{y_n}$, and\n$U = U_{y_1} \\cap \\dots \\cap U_{y_n}$ is the open set wanted.",
   "attrs": {}},
  {"source":
   {"file": "blueprint/spaces/compact/thm-fip.proof.md", "anonymous": false},
   "kind": "proof",
   "id": "proof/thm-fip",
   "depth": 1,
   "boundary": [{"role": "of", "id": "thm-fip"}],
   "body":
   "Both directions are the contrapositive of each other once the complements\nare taken: [lem-complements] exchanges the two conditions, and\n[lem-finite-subfamily] says what a finite subcover becomes.",
   "attrs": {}},
