  {"source": {"file": "blueprint/products/rem-infinite.md", "anonymous": false},
   "kind": "remark",
   "id": "rem-infinite",
   "depth": 0,
   "boundary": [],
   "body":
   "For an arbitrary family $(X_\\alpha)_{\\alpha \\in A}$ the statement is\nTychonoff's theorem, which needs the axiom of choice; the argument above\nonly gives finite products, by induction on the number of factors:\n$\\prod_{k=1}^{n+1} X_k \\cong \\bigl(\\prod_{k=1}^{n} X_k\\bigr) \\times X_{n+1}$.",
   "attrs": {"title": "Arbitrary products", "order": 2}},
  {"source": {"file": "blueprint/spaces/_section.md", "anonymous": false},
   "kind": "section",
   "id": "spaces",
   "depth": 0,
   "boundary": [],
   "body":
   "The vocabulary of covers, and the characterisation of compactness by closed\nsets.",
   "attrs": {"title": "Covers and compact spaces", "order": 2}},
  {"source":
   {"file": "blueprint/spaces/compact/thm-fip.md", "anonymous": false},
   "kind": "theorem",
   "id": "thm-fip",
   "depth": 0,
   "boundary": [],
   "body":
   "$X$ is compact if and only if every family $(F_i)_{i \\in I}$ of closed\nsubsets of $X$ with the finite intersection property has\n$\\bigcap_{i \\in I} F_i \\neq \\emptyset$.",
   "attrs": {"title": "Compactness by closed sets", "order": 3}},
  {"source": {"file": "blueprint/products/thm-product.md", "anonymous": false},
   "kind": "theorem",
   "id": "thm-product",
   "depth": 0,
   "boundary": [],
   "body":
   "If $X$ and $Y$ are compact, so is $X \\times Y$ with the product topology.\n\n## Proof\n\nLet $\\fam{W}$ be an open cover of $X \\times Y$.  For each $x \\in X$ the\nslice $\\{x\\} \\times Y \\cong Y$ is compact, so finitely many members of\n$\\fam{W}$ cover it; call their union $W_x$.  By [lem-tube] there is an open\n$U_x \\ni x$ with $U_x \\times Y \\subseteq W_x$.\n\n1. The $U_x$ cover $X$, so by [def-compact] finitely many do:\n   $U_{x_1}, \\dots, U_{x_m}$.\n2. Then $X \\times Y = \\bigcup_{k=1}^{m} U_{x_k} \\times Y \\subseteq \\bigcup_k W_{x_k}$,\n   a union of finitely many members of $\\fam{W}$.\n\nCompare the closed-set form, [thm-fip], which gives the same result by a\nless direct route.",
   "attrs": {"title": "Products of two compact spaces", "order": 1}},
  {"source":
